      "name": "Operation Endgame malware takedown turns up over 6 million stolen logins",
      "description": "Police in nine countries, working with Europol, took down servers behind the Gootloader, CastleRAT and StealC malware operations this week and recovered more than 6 million credentials stolen from infected computers. Europol announced the action as the latest round of Operation Endgame, the international campaign against the services that give ransomware gangs their way into a network.",
